<title>JAPAN: Mazda June exports up 51.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Mazda June exports up 51.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mazda Motor Corp said on Friday that its vehicle exports in June rose 51.3 percent from a year earlier to 51,880 units.</p>
<p>Domestic vehicle production rose 42.1 percent in June from a year earlier to 74,193 vehicles, Mazda said.  </p>
<p>Mazda's exports rose for the third straight month in June on a year-on-year basis, helped by the weaker yen and good demand in the United States and Europe for its 323 compact car, MPV minivan, Millenia luxury sedan and some other models, a Mazda spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Its domestic production rose for the fourth consecutive month in June, helped by higher domestic sales and exports.  </p>
<p>Mazda's domestic vehicle production, exports and domestic sales in June were as follows (with percentage comparisons from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Production	   74,193  up   42.1 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		 58,447  up   58.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     15,746  up    2.2 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     30,033  up   23.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		 20,218  up   55.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus	9,815  down 13.5 percent</p>
<p> Exports		51,880  up   51.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		 41,825  up   45.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     10,055  up   82.7 percent</p>
<p>The breakdown of January-June period was:</p>
<p> Production	  445,501  up   14.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		346,591  up   14.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     98,910  up   14.4 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales    188,430  up   12.0 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		124,692  up   32.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     63,738  down 14.3 percent</p>
<p> Exports	     274,867  up   15.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		228,570  up   12.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     46,297  up   37.5 percent</p>
</text>
